    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-eb868e9d06c1\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"no-increment-narration-comment\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"^\\\\s*(//|/\\\\*|\\\\*)\\\\s*([Ii]ncrement|[Dd]ecrement|[Ii]ncrease|[Dd]ecrease) (the )?[A-Za-z_.]+( by (1|one))?\\\\s*(\\\\*/)?\\\\s*$\",\"path\":\".floor/added-lines.txt\"},{\"id\":\"no-loop-narration-comment\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"^\\\\s*(//|/\\\\*|\\\\*)\\\\s*([Ll]oop|[Ii]terate|[Mm]ap|[Ss]witch) (over|through|on) [A-Za-z_.]+( [A-Za-z_.]+)?\\\\s*(\\\\*/)?\\\\s*$\",\"path\":\".floor/added-lines.txt\"}],\"coverage\":\"Added comment lines that consist only of a stock narration of an increment or decrement ('// increment count'). Also added comment lines that consist only of a short loop, map or switch narration of at most two words after the verb ('// loop over items', '// switch on kind').\",\"residual\":\"Does any comment added by this edit merely restate what the adjacent code line already shows, such as its operation, control flow or names, rather than explaining why or adding information not visible in the code?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/util/counter.ts b/src/util/counter.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/util/counter.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\\n+export function bump(count: number): number {\\n+  // increment count\\n+  return count + 1;\\n+}\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/util/total.ts b/src/util/total.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/util/total.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\\n+export function total(items: number[]): number {\\n+  let sum = 0;\\n+  // loop over items\\n+  for (const item of items) {\\n+    sum += item;\\n+  }\\n+  return sum;\\n+}\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/util/fees.ts b/src/util/fees.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/util/fees.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\\n+export function feeCents(amountCents: number): number {\\n+  // Callers pass cents; rounding here would double-count fees.\\n+  return Math.floor(amountCents * 0.03);\\n+}\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"Whether a comment restates its adjacent line is a judgement about meaning, and patterns match one line at a time, so they cannot see adjacency. The constraints only catch whole-line, boilerplate narration comments, which almost never carry a why. Every other restating comment needs judgement, so the class is partial.\"}",
